reports.query:
// CARD - "Pathao Pay drill-down" (report type: Graph)
//
// Parameter: $neodash_focus, set by clicking any node (property `click`).
// Unset  -> defaults to 'root', so the card opens on the Pathao Pay node.
//
// Reveal rule: show the focus node, its ancestors (the breadcrumb back
// to Pathao Pay) and its direct children. One click = one level deeper:
//
//   Pathao Pay -> Customers -> C1..Cn -> Customer-<acc> -> TXN_TYPE_D_C
//     -> Credit -> P2P / TOP UP / CASH OUT / ... -> Customer-<acc> + END
//     -> Debit  -> TXN_TYPE -> P2P / TOP UP / ...  -> Customer-<acc> + END
//
// The level-10 fan-out stops once the counterparty amounts balance the
// transaction type's total; the END node marks that point. Clicking END
// sets focus back to 'root' because its `click` property holds 'root' -
// which is the cycle.
//
// STALE FOCUS. NeoDash keeps `neodash_focus` in browser localStorage, so
// it survives a rebuild of the tree. Rebuilding renames keys, and a
// focus pointing at a key that no longer exists would match nothing and
// draw an EMPTY CARD with no error - which looks exactly like a broken
// dashboard. The OPTIONAL MATCH below falls back to 'root' in that case,
// so a stale parameter costs you the drill-down position and nothing else.
// PAGING AT LEVEL 2. All 38 customer pages hang off the root, but only
// page 1 is revealed automatically - otherwise Pathao Pay would fan out
// into 38 near-identical nodes. Pages 2+ are reached only by clicking
// the page node, whose `click` points at the next page, so the level
// behaves like one node cycling through tens rather than a fan-out.
WITH coalesce($neodash_focus, 'root') AS fk
OPTIONAL MATCH (stale:Nav {key: fk})
WITH CASE WHEN stale IS NULL THEN 'root' ELSE fk END AS fk
MATCH (f:Nav {key: fk})
MATCH (n:Nav)
WHERE f.path STARTS WITH n.path      // ancestors of the focus, and the focus itself
   OR (n.parent_key = f.key          // the focus node's direct children ...
       AND (NOT n:CustomerPage OR n.page = 1))   // ... but only page 1 of them
WITH collect(DISTINCT n) AS shown
UNWIND shown AS a
MATCH p = (a)-[:EXPANDS]->(b)
WHERE b IN shown
RETURN p

// CARD - "Transactions" (report type: Table)
// Every column of the source table, exactly as supplied.
//
// DYNAMIC: the table follows whichever node is selected in the graph.
// Each Nav node carries four filter properties written by
// cypher/03_build_nav_graph.cypher, and this card applies whichever of
// them are set:
//
//   f_acc   STATEMENT_FOR_ACC  - set from the C1..Cn level downwards
//   f_dc    TXN_TYPE_D_C       - set from Credit / Debit downwards
//   f_type  TXN_TYPE           - set on P2P / TOP UP / CASH OUT / ...
//   f_cp    TXN_WITH_ACC       - set on the level-10 Customer-<acc> nodes
//
// So: Pathao Pay or Customers -> everything (sampled); C3 -> that
// customer's rows; Debit -> only their debits; CASH OUT -> only their
// cash-out debits; Customer-1728... -> only the rows between the two.
//
// The LIMIT matters: with millions of rows loaded, an unbounded table
// card will hang the browser. Raise it if you want - the browser, not
// Neo4j, is what struggles first.
// A focus key that no longer exists (after a rebuild renames keys) leaves
// every filter null, which shows the unfiltered sample - the same thing
// 'root' shows. See the note in card2_expansion_graph.cypher.
WITH coalesce($neodash_focus, 'root') AS fk
OPTIONAL MATCH (f:Nav {key: fk})
WITH f.f_acc AS f_acc, f.f_dc AS f_dc, f.f_type AS f_type, f.f_cp AS f_cp
MATCH (t:Transaction)
WHERE (f_acc  IS NULL OR t.stmt_acc     = f_acc)
  AND (f_dc   IS NULL OR t.txn_type_d_c = f_dc)
  AND (f_type IS NULL OR t.txn_type     = f_type)
  AND (f_cp   IS NULL OR t.with_acc     = f_cp)
RETURN t.unq_id        AS UNQ_ID,
       t.from_date     AS FROM_DATE,
       t.to_date       AS TO_DATE,
       t.serial_no     AS SerialNo,
       t.txn_date_time AS TXN_DATE_TIME,
       t.txn_id        AS TXN_ID,
       t.txn_type      AS TXN_TYPE,
       t.account_type  AS ACCOUNT_TYPE,
       t.stmt_acc      AS STATEMENT_FOR_ACC,
       t.with_acc      AS TXN_WITH_ACC,
       t.channel       AS CHANNEL,
       t.reference     AS REFERENCE,
       t.txn_type_d_c  AS TXN_TYPE_D_C,
       t.status        AS STATUS,
       t.amount        AS TXN_AMT,
       t.balance_after AS AVAILABLE_BLC_AFTER_TXN,
       t.txn_with_info AS TXN_WITH_INFO
ORDER BY STATEMENT_FOR_ACC, TXN_DATE_TIME, SerialNo
LIMIT 2000
